# Reply in Chat, Not in the Project

Do **not** answer the user’s prompts, questions, or requests by writing into the project.

Forbidden places for agent↔user replies or meta notes:

- Code comments, docstrings, TODOs, `# NOTE for user`, commit-message asides to the user
- UI strings, labels, tooltips, empty states, placeholders
- README / docs / PR descriptions used as a chat substitute
- Log messages or debug prints meant for the user instead of the conversation

Respond in the **chat** (and only put in the repo what the product/codebase actually needs).

```text
❌ BAD: // Per your request we skip region X — see chat
❌ BAD: UI label "Waiting for your approval to reload"
✅ GOOD: Answer in chat; code/UI stay product-facing only
```
